## Features

### 🗺️ Map and City Footprints
- Nationwide city-boundary GeoJSON (parsed in an isolate) with ray-casting hit tests.
- Long-press a city to light it up / un-light it, plan a trip, or open trip records; lit cities render as highlighted polygons.
- Lighting up auto-creates a travel archive; bills, notes and itineraries are filed by city.

### 🧭 AI Trip Planning
- Slot filling with the small LLM + RAG few-shot examples: extracts departure city, destination, days and budget from one sentence.
- A deterministic DFS planning engine (time-driven state machine + backtracking pruning + dynamic budget splitting) plans against real attraction / train / flight data — no more hallucinated train numbers or wrong totals.
- Outputs day-grouped timeline itinerary cards: transport / meals / hotels / attractions + itemized cost + over-budget alert.

### 💬 Smart Expense Logging
- Natural-language logging: say "Nanning accommodation 200" and it is categorized automatically.
- Query bill details and spending stats by city.

### 📚 Travel Guide Q&A
- Vector-search over a local travel-guide knowledge base; supports `.txt` / `.pdf` / `.csv` ingestion with incremental updates.

### 🛡️ Stable Dialogue (Harness Architecture)
- Deterministic Python code validates model outputs: passes valid answers straight through, removes failed sub-agents and re-routes.
- A stable conversational experience even on a 0.8B parameter model.

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[Web Frontend Vue 3] -->|HTTP / SSE| B[FastAPI Backend]
    B --> C{Supervisor Router}
    C -->|Trip| D[travel sub-agent]
    C -->|Operation| E[operation sub-agent]
    C -->|Chat| F[chat sub-agent]
    D -->|Planning| D1[Slot filling LLM+RAG]
    D1 --> D2[DFS planning engine]
    D -->|Guide Q| D3[RAG guide Q&A]
    E --> E1[Billing / Cities / Bills]
    D2 & D3 & E1 --> G[harness validation]
    G -->|OK| H[to user]
    G -->|Fail| C
```

One planning request end-to-end:

```
User: "Plan 4 days in Hangzhou from Shanghai, budget 3000"
  → supervisor picks the travel sub-agent
  → slot filling: {from:Shanghai, to:Hangzhou, days:4, budget:3000}
  → DFS engine: (outbound × return × hotel) combos + fill day by day
  → returns timeline itinerary card
```

## Tech Stack

| Layer   | Technology |
|---------|------------|
| Frontend | Vue 3 + TypeScript + Vite + naive-ui + Leaflet (AMap / Esri tiles, AMap JS API v2) |
| Backend | FastAPI + SQLAlchemy 2.0(async) + MySQL 8.x + Redis + Alembic |
| Agents | LangChain create_agent + LangGraph, multi-agent supervisor |
| Planner | Custom DFS + backtracking pruning + dynamic budget splitting |
| RAG | ChromaDB + m3e embeddings |
| Model | Qwen3.5-0.8B LoRA fine-tune (LLaMA-Factory) + llama.cpp local inference |

## Project Structure

```
footprint/
├── backend/
│   ├── main.py                    # entrypoint (uvicorn main:app)
│   ├── alembic/
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── routers/               # user / cities / trips / bills / agent ...
│   │   ├── services/
│   │   ├── crud/
│   │   ├── models/
│   │   ├── config/                # DB / mail / JWT (reads .env)
│   │   ├── core/
│   │   ├── data/                  # runtime data cache (gitignored)
│   │   └── agent/                 # multi-agent system
│   │       ├── footprint_agent.py  # harness loop + direct channels + intent routing
│   │       ├── middleware.py      # harness middleware (verdict / abort / write gate)
│   │       ├── constraints.py     # harness constraints (write auth / evidence / claims)
│   │       ├── prompts/
│   │       ├── config/
│   │       ├── data/              # slot examples + guide corpus (regenerate via script)
│   │       ├── model/             # model factory (llama.cpp)
│   │       ├── chat/
│   │       ├── operation/         # software-operation sub-agent (bills / cities / memory)
│   │       └── travel/            # planner engine / RAG / slot filler / data sources
│   ├── train_data/                # fine-tuning data
│   └── scripts/                   # tooling (KB build / finetune data / regression tests)
├── finetune/                      # LLaMA-Factory configs
└── web/                           # Vue 3 web frontend
    └── src/                       # views / components / stores / api / utils
```

## Requirements

| Dependency | Version | Purpose |
|------------|---------|---------|
| Python | 3.12+ | Backend runtime |
| [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) | latest | Python dependency manager |
| MySQL | 8.x | Database |
| Redis | 6+ | CAPTCHA cooldown / cache |
| Node.js | 18+ | Frontend build |
| [llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp) | latest | Local model inference |
| Fine-tuned dialogue model | Qwen3.5-0.8B GGUF | port 8080 |
| [m3e-small](https://huggingface.co/moka-ai/m3e-small) GGUF | - | embedding, port 8081 |

## Quick Start

> Commands run from the project root unless noted; backend commands first `cd backend`.

### 1. Configure Backend

```bash
cd backend
uv sync
cp .env.example .env        # then fill in your own keys
```

See [Configuration Reference](#configuration-reference) for every variable.

### 2. Initialize Database

Create a `footprint` database in MySQL (utf8mb4), then:

```bash
alembic upgrade head
```

### 3. Start the Two Local Model Services

Two model servers are required — both must be running:

```bash
# Terminal 1: dialogue model (port 8080) — slot filling, routing, chat
llama-server -m qwen3.5-0.8b.gguf --port 8080

# Terminal 2: embedding model (port 8081) — guides & slot examples, needs --embedding
llama-server -m m3e-small.gguf --port 8081 --embedding
```

Mappings live in `backend/app/agent/config/model.yml`.

### 4. Build the Vector Database

Required once before first use, otherwise guide Q&A and slot filling are empty:

```bash
# ① Ingest slot-filling few-shot examples
python scripts/_load_slots.py

# ② Ingest guide docs (.txt/.pdf/.csv under backend/app/agent/data/)
python -c "from app.agent.travel.services.vector_store import VectorStoreService; VectorStoreService().load_document()"
```

- Stored under `backend/chroma_db/`; incremental via MD5, safe to re-run.
- Add more guides by dropping `.txt` (per city) / `.pdf` / `.csv` files into
  `backend/app/agent/data/` and re-running ②.

### 5. Start the Backend

```bash
uvicorn main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
```

### 6. Start the Frontend

```bash
cd web
npm install
npm run dev            # dev server at http://localhost:5173 (/api proxied to 8000)
```

Production build runs in a container: `docker compose --profile web up -d frontend` (nginx, <http://localhost:8080>).

## Usage Guide

### Plan a Trip
Say "Plan 4 days in Hangzhou from Shanghai, budget 3000" → a 4-day itinerary card
with trains, meals, hotels, activities, itemized costs and over-budget alerts.

### Log an Expense
Traveling, say "Nanning accommodation 200" → auto-categorized; ask anytime
"how much did I spend in Nanning" to view bills.

### Light Up a City
Long-press a city you visited → Light up → travel archive created automatically;
bills / notes / itineraries are filed by city, and the city highlights on the map.

## Fine-tune Your Own Model

The prompts and interaction design can be reproduced with any base model:

1. Training data: `backend/train_data/tool_calling_train.jsonl`
   (use `backend/scripts/gen_finetune_data.py` to append samples; read the script header first)
2. LoRA fine-tune Qwen3.5-0.8B with [LLaMA-Factory](https://github.com/hiyouga/LLaMA-Factory)
   (sharegpt / tool-calling format)
3. Merge the LoRA weights, export to GGUF, deploy with llama.cpp (see Step 3)
4. Run `backend/scripts/batch_test_budget.py` for regression.

## Configuration Reference

All `backend/.env` variables:

| Variable | Description | Example |
|----------|-------------|---------|
| AMAP_KEY | Amap Open key (POI data) | - |
| ROLLINGGO_KEY | RollingGo key (transport data) | - |
| TIANDITU_KEYS | TiandiMap key(s), comma-separated for polling | key1,key2 |
| TENCENT_KEY | Tencent location key (city geocoding) | - |
| MAIL_USERNAME | Email sending the CAPTCHA codes | xxx@qq.com |
| MAIL_PASSWORD | QQ SMTP auth code (NOT the login password) | 16-char code |
| MAIL_FROM | Sender address (same as MAIL_USERNAME) | xxx@qq.com |
| MAIL_PORT | SMTP port (QQ SSL always 465) | 465 |
| MAIL_SERVER | SMTP server | smtp.qq.com |
| MAIL_SSL / MAIL_STARTTLS | Encryption | True / False |
| JWT_SECRET_KEY | Token signing secret, ≥32 bytes random | `python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"` |
| DB_USER / DB_PASSWORD | MySQL credentials | root / xxx |
| DB_HOST / DB_PORT | MySQL host / port | localhost / 3306 |
| DB_NAME | Database name | footprint |

Model / vector-DB configs are yml files under `backend/app/agent/config/`
(model.yml / chroma.yml / prompts.yml); usually no changes needed.

## FAQ

<details>
<summary><b>Login returns 500 / CAPTCHA not received?</b></summary>

Check MySQL is running, `footprint` exists, `alembic upgrade head` ran, and the SMTP settings in
`.env` are correct (use the SMTP **auth code**, not the QQ login password).
</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Guide Q&A / slot filling has no response?</b></summary>

The port-8081 embedding service may be down, or Step 4 wasn't run.
Confirm `backend/chroma_db/` exists and both model services are up.
</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Model connection errors / 502s?</b></summary>

Confirm both llama.cpp servers (8080 / 8081) are running; on Windows ten/httpx 502s
are worked around by the built-in `RequestsTransport` (see `backend/app/agent/model/factory.py`).
</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Plan says "cannot plan" or over budget?</b></summary>

A too-low budget triggers pruning (engine allows 20% tolerance). Raise the budget, or check the
logs to confirm POI / restaurant / transport data was fetched with valid keys.
</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Map tiles not showing?</b></summary>

TiandiMap key (TIANDITU_KEYS) missing or out of quota; multiple keys in `.env` are polled.
</details>

## Data Notice

This repository **does not include any business data**. On first run the app fetches attraction,
restaurant and transport data over the API keys in your `.env` (Amap / 12306 / RollingGo) and
caches it locally under `backend/app/data/` (excluded from git).

Data comes from third-party services; comply with their terms of service and do not redistribute it.

